<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cuts duty on hotel goods, pharmaceuticals.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cuts duty on hotel goods, pharmaceuticals.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan has slashed import duty on pharmaceutical raw material and hotel equipment, an official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Mohibullah Shah, secretary at the state-run Board of Investment, told a news conference that duty on pharmaceutical raw material had been trimmed to 10 percent from 25 percent to bring down soaring prices of medicines.</p>
<p>He said duty on hotel equipment, including refrigerators and kitchen items, had been reduced to 25 percent from 65 percent to promote tourism.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
</text>
